    "body": "## Purpose\n\n`(H200 MIG 35GB) PyTorch Fullgraph` takes about 55 min. It ran one pytest per file through `find | xargs`, which the runtime sharder can't plan, because it handles plain pytest commands only. This replaces that with one `pytest -s -v compile/fullgraph --ignore=compile/fullgraph/test_full_cudagraph.py` and sets `automatic_shard: true`, as in #60492 and the batches after it.\n\n- The per-file processes were a workaround for #28965 (\"Cannot re-initialize CUDA in forked subprocess\"). That issue is closed. The Buildkite run below checks that the files now pass in one process.\n- On current timings the generator plans 4 shards (est. 17.1 / 16.0 / 14.8 / 8.3 min) and splits `test_basic_correctness.py` by test function.\n- The AMD mirror keeps the `find | xargs` command as is.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nBuildkite build https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/94186, running only this step. I'll add wall time, GPU time and test counts against main here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
